<!-- EFV_Dev_Spike.xml (EFV_Dev 1.0.3.2, TESTING ONLY): the two hidden unit abilities of the veteran
     one-turn restore spike (V button, Scripts/EFV_Dev_Gameplay.lua "V Veteran spike").
     Both are Inactive: no unit has them until the spike grants one with
     pUnit:GetAbility():ChangeAbilityCount(type, 1) (PiratesScenario_UnitCommands.lua:661-662 pattern).
     TypeTags: the ability classes of the common land and naval combat units (the class list of
     ABILITY_FINEST_HOUR_FRIENDLY_TERRITORY in Expansion2_UnitAbilities.xml, plus the naval classes of
     ABILITY_SWASHBUCKLER_UNIT_ACTIVE / ABILITY_ERIKSON_NAVAL_SIGHT); a unit of another class cannot hold them.

     V1  EFV_DEV_ABILITY_PROMOTE_KEEP_MOVES: a promotion does not end the unit's turn. New modifier type
         with COLLECTION_OWNER (the unit that holds the ability) and the effect of the Gran Colombia trait
         (DLC/GranColombia_Maya/Data/GranColombia_Maya_Modifiers.xml:45-49
         MODIFIER_PLAYER_UNITS_PROMOTE_NO_FINISH_MOVES = COLLECTION_PLAYER_UNITS +
         EFFECT_ADJUST_UNIT_PROMOTE_NO_FINISH_MOVES; argument NoFinishMoves = true,
         GranColombia_Maya_Civilizations.xml TRAIT_PROMOTE_NO_FINISH_MOVES).
     V3  EFV_DEV_ABILITY_VET_LEVEL: level +3. The Giant Death Robot's ABILITY_UNIT_AUTO_VETERANCY pattern
         (DLC/Expansion2/Data/Expansion2_UnitAbilities.xml: GDR_VETERAN_NAME, ModifierType
         MODIFIER_PLAYER_UNIT_ADJUST_EXPERIENCE_LEVEL, argument Amount = 2; the modifier type is
         Base/Assets/Gameplay/Data/Modifiers.xml:1269-1273 = COLLECTION_OWNER +
         EFFECT_ADJUST_UNIT_EXPERIENCE_LEVEL). Amount 3 = the three promotions of the spike template. -->
